My First AI Portfolio Project Plan

###     Goal
I will build a lightweight, stateless AI Code Review Assistant as my first AI-integrated portfolio project using Next.js, Tailwind CSS, and the Gemini API. Instead of a generic chat box, my app will analyze code through three selectable reviewer personas (Strict Senior Dev, Friendly Tutor, and Algorithm Optimizer) and render a structured diagnostic dashboard showing Big-O complexity, breaking edge cases, categorized bug cards, and clean refactored code.

First Step
Use Gemini to help me draft a 3-step workflow:
1. Input: What data or trigger will start this?
2. Process: What AI tool or function will handle it?
3. Output: What should the result look like?

###     My Action Plan

Set Up My Project and Free API Key: I will initialize a Next.js (App Router) repository, install the Google Gen AI SDK, generate a free-tier API key from Google AI Studio, and store it in .env.local so my key stays hidden from the browser and GitHub.

Lock In My JSON Schema and Persona Prompts: I will define a strict JSON output structure and test my system prompts in Google AI Studio to ensure the AI consistently returns a 1–10 quality score, time/space complexity, edge cases, and refactored code in each persona's distinct voice.

Build the Backend API Proxy (/api/review): I will create a single server-side endpoint that validates incoming code snippets, attaches my secret API key, calls the Gemini API with enforced JSON schema output, and handles rate-limit or empty-input errors gracefully.

Build the Split-Screen Frontend UI: I will design a two-pane interface with a code editor, language selector, and persona toggle pills on the left, and an interactive dashboard on the right that displays severity badges, an edge-case breakdown table, and syntax-highlighted refactored code.

Polish for Visitors and Deploy Live: I will add a loading spinner, a 1-click "Copy Code" button, and 3 preset "Sample Buggy Code" buttons so recruiters can test the demo with one click, then deploy the app to Vercel and document the architecture in my GitHub README.

###      Skills I’ll Learn

AI API & Structured Output Engineering: I will learn how to integrate the @google/genai SDK, craft distinct persona system prompts, and enforce strict JSON schemas so the model behaves like a predictable backend service instead of an unstructured chatbot.

Secure Full-Stack API Proxying: I will learn how to build server-side Next.js App Router route handlers (app/api/.../route.js), keep secret credentials protected in .env.local, and handle input validation and API rate limits cleanly.  

Data-Driven Frontend UI Design: I will learn how to parse structured JSON responses in React and render interactive visual components—including score badges, Big-O pills, edge-case tables, loading states, and syntax-highlighted code blocks—styled with Tailwind CSS.

Version Control & Cloud Deployment: I will learn how to manage a clean Git repository with proper .gitignore rules, configure production environment variables in Vercel, and deploy a live full-stack app.

